<title>NETHERLANDS: WERELDHAVE H1 PROFIT RISES TO NLG 67.2 MLN.</title>
<headline>WERELDHAVE H1 PROFIT RISES TO NLG 67.2 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     4.09 vs   3.73</p>
<p>    Net profit (direct inv result)  67.2  vs  59</p>
<p>    Investment income		   94.5  vs  95.2</p>
<p>    Interest charges		    21.9  vs  28.3</p>
<p>    Tax					0.2  vs   0.1</p>
<p>    Operating costs			5.2  vs   7.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Property investment fund Wereldhave NV said that</p>
<p>based on stable average exchange rates at first-half levels, it</p>
<p>expected to achieve full-year profits per ordinary share of at</p>
<p>least 8.20 guilders, compared with a year-earlier 7.68 guilders.</p>
<p>It said in May it expected full-year earnings per share of some</p>
<p>7.90 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
